WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.780
The city of Dunedin Florida

00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:03.710
wants to take this man’s home.

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:06.050
Because I was tardy cutting the grass

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:09.220
Jim Dicken’s mom died so he went to South Carolina

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:11.700
to take care of her estate.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:15.680
City officials then started fining Ficken $500 a day

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:19.789
because his grass had grown longer than ten inches.

00:00:19.789 --> 00:00:21.939
Such fines add up.

00:00:21.939 --> 00:00:24.080
This is a letter, from the city attorney,

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:27.550
demanding $24,454 dollars

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:30.099
Now the fine is up to $30,000.

00:00:30.099 --> 00:00:31.599
That’s asinine!

00:00:31.599 --> 00:00:34.750
Ficken’s neighbor can’t believe he was fined so much.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:36.300
Just for grass!

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.860
Because Ficken doesn’t have $30,000,

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:41.260
the city says it will foreclose on his home

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:42.560
to collect the fine.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:43.590
I was shocked.

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:46.710
The town says you're kind of a public nuisance.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:50.320
I got everything fixed and taken care of

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:53.490
You only get it fixed after they send warning

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:55.860
after warning, the neighbors complain

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:57.460
I guess I'm kind of a slob.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:59.420
Why don't you just pay the fine?

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:01.100
$30,000.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:03.610
Do you have $30,000 lying around?

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:05.580
In every instance that the city asked him to

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.700
do something, Jim did it.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:11.049
Lawyer Ari Bargil is defending Ficken against Dunedin.

00:01:11.049 --> 00:01:13.229
The city has gone nuclear.

00:01:13.229 --> 00:01:18.100
$500 per day for the violation of having tall grass,

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:20.260
and now he's facing the loss of his home.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:21.120
[Nature]

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.680
Dunedin’s politicians wouldn’t talk to us.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:26.300
Instead, they paid 25,000

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:30.020
for this public relations firm to speak to the media.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:31.300
The new PR manager

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:35.399
costing taxpayers 25,000 dollars for just one month.

00:01:35.399 --> 00:01:36.440
The PP firms says,

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.520
“Dunedin has no desire to impose large fines”

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:41.140
their goal is just to

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:45.399
“ensure that Dunedin is a high-quality community”

00:01:45.399 --> 00:01:47.180
But if the politicians only cared about

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:48.899
the quality of the lawns

00:01:48.899 --> 00:01:50.720
They could have done what their own ordinances

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:54.540
permit them to do, which is hire a lawn service

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:56.180
to come out and mow the grass,

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:58.200
and send Jim a bill for 150 bucks,

00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.200
but they didn't do that.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.200
They could do that.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:02.529
They absolutely can do that, but they didn't do that.

00:02:02.529 --> 00:02:05.279
And that's because they prioritize revenue collection.

00:02:05.279 --> 00:02:06.499
They want the money.

00:02:06.499 --> 00:02:08.660
It's pretty apparent that code enforcement

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:10.840
is a major cash cow for the city of Dunedin.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:14.900
11 years ago Dunedin collected $34,000 in fines.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:18.530
Last year, $1.3 million

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:20.100
I got violated for a lawn mower in my yard

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.220
they violated me for a hole,

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:23.420
the size of a quarter, in my stucco.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:24.960
They find people they can pick on

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.480
and they then keep picking on them.

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:28.690
Dunedin put a lien on her house.

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:31.460
They say she owes them $32,000

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:33.420
I can’t tell you how many sleepless nights

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:36.120
I’ve had because of the city of Dunedin.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:37.840
Just try to think of what to say to them

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:39.380
just to have them leave me alone

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:41.080
The city is just a bunch of bullies,

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:44.000
and they expect people not to stand up to em’

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.340
because to stand up to em’

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:47.260
requires expensive legal help.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:49.620
Ficken managed to get that legal help for free

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:51.680
from the Institute for Justice,

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:54.120
a law firm that defends individuals

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:55.730
abused by governments.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:57.600
[Music]

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:00.340
Its lawyers, portraying themselves in this video as

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:02.980
western heroes ready to punish bad guys,

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:05.340
say many cities now pad their budgets

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:07.470
by imposing excessive fines.

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:09.720
A North Carolina city fined a local church

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:13.730
$100 a branch for excessive tree pruning.

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:15.520
Private citizens are being, essentially,

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:17.460
extorted by their governments,

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:20.080
and fined incredible amounts of money

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:21.980
for really, really small violations.

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:23.680
And if you can’t pay the fine,

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:25.300
they’ll take your home.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:27.000
The city of Dunedin code enforcement board

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.990
authorized the city’s attorney’s office

00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:31.110
to file foreclosure actions.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.080
The City Attorney of Dunedin, in the last year,

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:37.370
has sought permission to foreclose on 18 properties.

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:38.880
That violates the 8th amendment,

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:40.990
says the Institute for Justice.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:42.560
It not only protects us from

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:44.620
cruel and unusual punishment,

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:46.740
But right next to that 8th Amendment is a

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:50.400
protection to be free from excessive fines.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.420
Our Founders, they recognized that the ability to fine

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:55.710
is the ability to cripple.

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:57.540
It's one of the ways, other than incarceration,

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:59.370
that government can really oppress.

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:02.180
If governments can, they will.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:04.940
So we should be grateful for the 8th amendment.

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:07.260
It protects us from excessive fines and

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:09.460
what’s more excessive than politicians

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:12.620
taking your home because you didn’t cut your grass?

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:15.960
[Mower sounds]

